### Reproduction matrix

- OnePlus phone (OnePlus8T), Android 14: reproducible
- Official Android 14 emulator: not reproducible
- Default Flutter-generated manifest: not reproducible
- Same app with `android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback="true"`: reproducible on affected device

### Steps to reproduce

1. Create a new Flutter app with `flutter create bug`.
2. Replace `lib/main.dart` with the minimal sample below.
3. Run the app on a physical OnePlus device running Android 14.
4. Verify that the app behaves normally with the default Flutter-generated manifest.
5. Add `android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback="true"` to the `<application>` tag in `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`.
6. Rebuild and run the same app on the same OnePlus device.
7. Navigate to the second page.
8. Perform the predictive back gesture.
9. Observe that the page becomes unresponsive / back behavior breaks.

I cannot reproduce this issue on the official Android 14 emulator; so far I can only reproduce it on some OEM devices such as OnePlus phones.

### Expected results

The app should continue to handle back navigation correctly after enabling predictive back through `android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback="true"`. Enabling this documented configuration should not make the page unresponsive or break route popping.

### Actual results

With the default Flutter-generated manifest, I cannot reproduce the issue on the same device. After explicitly adding `android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback="true"`, the issue reproduces consistently on my OnePlus Android 14 device.

I cannot reproduce the issue on the official Android 14 emulator.

