### Use case

When having a SingleChildScrollView with `scrollDirection: Axis.horizontal`, it is currently not possible to scroll it if having the following setup (at least):

- Web (Tested with Firefox and Chrome) on MacOS (but would be interesting, if its the same behavior on all other (desktop) platforms)
- a regular mouse (no trackpad, no horizontal scroll buttons)

Example:
```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() => runApp(const MyApp());

class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
  const MyApp({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      title: 'Flutter Demo',
      debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false,
      theme: ThemeData(colorSchemeSeed: Colors.blue),
      home: const MyHomePage(title: 'Flutter Demo Home Page'),
    );
  }
}

class MyHomePage extends StatefulWidget {
  final String title;

  const MyHomePage({super.key, required this.title});

  @override
  State<MyHomePage> createState() => _MyHomePageState();
}

class _MyHomePageState extends State<MyHomePage> {
  int _counter = 0;

  void _incrementCounter() {
    setState(() {
      _counter++;
    });
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(title: Text(widget.title)),
      body: Center(
        child: SizedBox(
          height: 300,
          width: 300,
          child: Column(
            mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,
            children: [
              SingleChildScrollView(
                  scrollDirection: Axis.horizontal,
                  child: Row(
                    mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,
                    spacing: 8,
                    children: List.generate(9, (i) => Container(width: 100, height: 50, color: Colors.red)),

                  ),
                ),
              Expanded(
                child: SingleChildScrollView(
                scrollDirection: Axis.vertical,
                child: Column(
                  mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,
                  spacing: 8,
                  children: List.generate(9, (i) => Container(width: 100, height: 50, color: Colors.blue)),
                ),
              ), 
              ),
            ],
          ),
        ),
      ),
      floatingActionButton: FloatingActionButton(
        onPressed: _incrementCounter,
        tooltip: 'Increment',
        child: const Icon(Icons.add),
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

- One can scroll the vertical scroll with the scroll wheel
- One cannot scroll the horizontal scroll with the scroll wheel (even with shift pressed)
- One drag (with mouse click) to move the items in the scroll view.

### Proposal

- Allow scrolling a horizontal `SingleChildScrollView` with a the vertical mouse scroll wheel, but only if its not wrapped in a Vertical Scroll View.
- Allow always horizontal scroll if pressing `shift` + vertical scroll.
- Optional: allow dragging scrolls on desktop environments

Workaround:
- user uses trackpad, or input device with horizontal scroll buttons / wheel.

Related:
https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues/105095

### Steps to reproduce

1) Run code snippet on web
2) Focus on any element with tab traversal (Tab key)
3) Focus on previous element with tab traversal (shift + Tab), it's easiest to reproduce that way, but sometimes even not necessary
4) Click on "Toggle can request focus" button to disable "Focus.canRequestFocus" for all the children.
5) Observe that focus is moved to another focus node, which should not be possible, because that node has "Focus.canRequestFocus == false"

### Expected results

Focus widgets with `canRequestFocus==false` can not get focus, the focus is lost, all of Focus widgets with `canRequestFocus==false` do not have primaryFocus.

### Actual results

a random Focus with `canRequestFocus==false` gets primary focus.

### Code sample

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(const MyApp());
}

class MyApp extends StatefulWidget {
  const MyApp({super.key});

  @override
  State<MyApp> createState() => _MyAppState();
}

class _MyAppState extends State<MyApp> {
  bool _canRequestFocus = true;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => MaterialApp(
        home: Scaffold(
          body: Column(
            crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,
            children: [
              ElevatedButton(
                onPressed: () {
                  setState(() {
                    _canRequestFocus = !_canRequestFocus;
                  });
                },
                child: Text('Toggle can request focus'),
              ),
              Column(
                children: List.generate(
                  10,
                  (i) => _FocusableChild(canRequestFocus: _canRequestFocus),
                ),
              ),
            ],
          ),
        ),
      );
}

class _FocusableChild extends StatelessWidget {
  const _FocusableChild({required this.canRequestFocus});

  final bool canRequestFocus;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Focus(
        canRequestFocus: canRequestFocus,
        child: Builder(builder: (context) {
          final focus = Focus.of(context);
          return Container(
            decoration: BoxDecoration(
              border:
                  focus.hasPrimaryFocus ? Border.all(color: Colors.blue) : null,
            ),
            child: Text(' canRequestFocus:${focus.canRequestFocus} '),
          );
        }),
      );
}
```

